post.description:
 This method schedules a Data Import Job to validation by creating a process associated to the job.

 Validation implies the execution of the job itself. This means that the mapped sheets and colums are processed, all data is read and business rules verified.

 The execution produces feedback information that is associated to the process.

 <b>The difference between Validation and Load is that with the Validation all data is analyzed but not stored. With Load all records are persisted.</b><br /><b>ScheduleTime</b> is optional, if not provided the jobs will execute with the actual date.<br /><br /><b>Example with scheduled time</b>

 	{
			"DataImportJobId": 338,
			"ScheduleTime": "2025-10-10T10:55:25.4477652-04:00"
	}
 <br /><b>Example to send the execution inmediatelly</b><br />

 	{
			"DataImportJobId": 338
	}

 This method schedules a Data Import Job to Load by creating a process associated to the job.

 Load implies the execution of the job itself. This means that the mapped sheets and colums are processed, all data is read, entities created and business rules verified.

 The execution produces feedback information that is associated to the process.

 <b>The difference between Validation and Load is that with the Validation all data is analyzed but not stored. With Load all records are persisted.</b><b>ScheduleTime</b> is optional, if not provided the jobs will execute with the actual date.<br /><br /><b>Example with scheduled time</b>

 	{
			"DataImportJobId": 338,
			"ScheduleTime": "2025-10-10T10:55:25.4477652-04:00"
	}
 <br /><b>Example to send the execution inmediatelly</b><br />

 	{
			"DataImportJobId": 338
	}
